            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0757" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.933/159: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-10-26T16:00:00-05:00">October 26, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>351. Your 927, October 25, 5 p.m., particularly paragraph 4.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The delay which you suggest is approved. I wish to be altogether
                        considerate of the views and convenience of the other Powers. See
                        Department’s 342, October 22, 5 p.m., last paragraph.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Further reply to your telegram under reference will follow.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
